# Documentation & Visual Ergonomics Standard (Q.E.D.)

When authoring documentation, diagrams, or visual assets in this repository:

## 1. Audience Separation
- **`README.md` (Human)**: Scannable in 60s. Start with the concrete problem, show Before/After code contrast, keep main text concise, and offload deep tables to `docs/`.
- **`AI_README.md` / `llms.txt` (Machine)**: Maximum token density, zero conversational fluff, explicit invariants, and exact file structure mappings.
- **Zero Emoji Salad**: Never prepend every header with cartoon emojis.

## 2. Diagram Ergonomics (Ban on Diagram Slop)
- **Strict Ban on 3-Screen Vertical Noodles**: Never generate multi-subgraph vertical Mermaid diagrams (`flowchart TD`) that create 2000px gray towers.
- **Horizontal & Compact**: Inline workflow diagrams must be horizontal (`flowchart LR`, SVGs) and stay under 150px in vertical height.
- **Evidence Over Abstract Art**: Prefer real terminal command and test logs showing Red/Green cycles over abstract diagrams.

## 3. High-Assurance SVG Standard
- **Pure Vector**: Responsive `viewBox="0 0 W H"` with `width="100%" height="auto" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"`.
- **Theme Immunity**: Include an outer canvas card container (`fill="url(#canvasGrad)" rx="14"`) so contrast is 100% stable in both Dark and Light themes.
- **Typography**: Use modern system font stacks (`-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI`).
- **Badges**: Use `style=flat-square` shields with calibrated color tokens.
